The Scott topology on the two-point lattice of propositions is the Sierpiński topology generated by the singleton of true.

The singleton of true is Scott-open: it is an upper set, and a directed supremum equals true only when some member is true. Conversely, a Scott-open set is empty, the singleton of true, or the whole space, according as it contains true and whether it contains false, and each of those three sets is Sierpiński-open.
